{"archetypes":[{"name":"stale-ref-hunter","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan deletes or renames ~10 symbols/files; downstream readers outside the explicit file list may silently break if not also updated.","prompt_body":"Search the full repository for every reference to the symbols and files this plan deletes or renames: `workflow_path`, `quick_mode`, `sketch_budget`, `review_budget`, `design_classification_source`, `design_classification_reason`, `TRIVIAL_DOC_ONLY`, `NO_SKETCHES_CLASSIFIED_TRIVIAL`, `--trivial`, `invoke-plan-validator-if-not-quick.sh`, `read-design-review-budget.sh`, `plan-review-quick.md`, and `test-read-design-review-budget-invoke`. For each hit, determine whether the containing file appears in the plan's files-to-modify list; flag every file that is NOT listed and whose reference would become dangling after the plan is applied. Pay particular attention to Makefiles, test-runner harnesses, CI config files, structural-test scripts that grep for literal strings, and documentation that cross-links to these symbols. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"deletion-completeness","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan deletes four files and renames one script without confirming that Makefiles, test registries, or link-checker manifests referencing those targets are also covered.","prompt_body":"For each file the plan marks DELETED (`skills/design/references/plan-review-quick.md`, `skills/design/scripts/read-design-review-budget.sh`, `skills/design/scripts/test-read-design-review-budget-invoke.sh`, `skills/design/scripts/test-read-design-review-budget-invoke.md`) and for the renamed script (`invoke-plan-validator-if-not-quick.sh` → `invoke-plan-validator.sh`), check whether the old path appears in: the root `Makefile`, any `GNUmakefile` or `*.mk` fragment, `scripts/test-design-structure.sh`, `scripts/relevant-checks.sh`, `agent-lint.toml`, any CI workflow under `.github/`, and any doc that a link-checker would validate. Verify the plan's modification list covers each such reference site and flag any site that is not listed. Also confirm the new filename `invoke-plan-validator.sh` does not collide with an existing file. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"counter-contract","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The Gate C per-tier re-run cap introduces a new `review-round-count.txt` counter whose writer/reader contract, initialization path, and interaction with the existing `plan-review-loop.sh --round-num` arg are underspecified in the plan.","prompt_body":"Examine the Gate C counter protocol for `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/review-round-count.txt` by reading the current `plan-review-loop.sh` and `plan-review-loop.md` to determine what `--round-num` does today and whether the script already tracks or writes a round counter internally. Verify that the plan's proposed increment site (Step 3 entry block in SKILL.md) and the cap-check read site (Gate C in `approval-gates.md`) are mutually consistent and do not double-count if `plan-review-loop.sh` also maintains state. Check whether the absent-file-treated-as-zero rule is specified at every read site in the plan (SKILL.md, approval-gates.md, and any helper) or only in the edge-cases section. Confirm that the hide-option behavior (omit 'Re-run review panel' at cap) is consistently described across SKILL.md, `approval-gates.md`, and the loop script contract, and that no code path can reach Gate C without the counter file having been created. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
